  "narration": {
    "title": "The Cubs and Rangers Make Their Move",
    "intro": "The Dodgers are still on top, but the action this week is in the middle of the board. The Cubs and Rays surged on hot last-ten runs, while the Braves and Yankees both stumbled to 3-7 and gave back ground.",
    "power_lead": "Los Angeles sits comfortably at number one, 54-30 with a run differential of plus-152 nobody else is near. The real climbers are the Cubs, up three to third on an 8-2 stretch, and the Rangers, who leapt 14 spots to ninth at .500 despite a minus-8 differential. Atlanta and New York remain strong on paper, plus-88 and plus-101, but a 3-7 last ten dropped them to seventh and eighth."
